  "content": {
    "id": "p52-q31-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "31",
    "prompt": "If 5 is added to both the numerator and denominator of a fraction, the result simplifies to $\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nIf 1 is subtracted from both the numerator and denominator, the result simplifies to $\\frac{1}{3}$.\n\nWhat was the original fraction?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{3}{7}$",
      "worked": "Let $p$ be the numerator and $q$ the denominator.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{p+5}{q+5} &= \\frac{2}{3} \\\\\n3p+15 &= 2q+10 \\\\\n3p-2q &= -5 \\qquad (1) \\\\\n\\frac{p-1}{q-1} &= \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n3p-3 &= q-1 \\\\\nq &= 3p-2 \\qquad (2)\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute (2) into (1).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n3p-2(3p-2) &= -5 \\\\\n3p-6p+4 &= -5 \\\\\n-3p &= -9 \\\\\np &= 3 \\\\\nq &= 3(3)-2 \\\\\nq &= 7\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original fraction was $\\frac{3}{7}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
